-- The stratification fixture: a cycle THROUGH a negation.
--
-- `p holds` depends negatively on `q holds`, which depends negatively on
-- `p holds`, so the two sit in one strongly-connected component containing a
-- negative edge — the Apt–Blair–Walker definition of unstratified.
--
-- __This module lowers successfully.__ It belongs beside the positive seeds and
-- NOT under not-ok/, because 'RStratification' is RECORDED, never enforced:
-- swipl rejects a non-stratified program, Blawx rejects it in v1, and ASP treats
-- non-stratification as the source of the multiple stable models that are the
-- entire point of that leg. Turning it into a LowerError in the middle-end would
-- break the ASP leg before it exists. The assertion this fixture carries is on
-- the `stratification:` block of the render, not on a failure.

DECLARE Flag HAS
    seed IS A BOOLEAN

@export
GIVEN f IS A Flag
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `p holds` IF
    f's seed AND NOT `q holds` f

@export
GIVEN f IS A Flag
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `q holds` IF
    NOT `p holds` f
